# Bump Plugin Version on Every Change

Whenever you modify any plugin code (PHP, assets, admin UI, blockers, etc.), you MUST bump the plugin version in the **same change**.

## Version locations (keep all in sync)

Update all three to the same new version:

1. Plugin header in `dn-controller.php` — `* Version: X.Y.Z`
2. Constant in `dn-controller.php` — `DN_CONTROLLER_VERSION`
3. Class constant in `includes/class-dn-controller.php` — `DN_Controller::VERSION`

## How to bump

- Patch (`1.1.0` → `1.1.1`): bug fixes, small rules, copy/UI tweaks
- Minor (`1.1.1` → `1.2.0`): new features / new blocker rules
- Major (`1.2.0` → `2.0.0`): breaking changes

## Checklist before finishing

- [ ] All three version strings match
- [ ] Version is higher than the previous one
- [ ] Do not leave version unchanged after code edits

```php
// ❌ BAD — code changed, version left as-is
* Version: 1.1.0
define('DN_CONTROLLER_VERSION', '1.1.0');
const VERSION = '1.1.0';

// ✅ GOOD — code changed + version bumped together
* Version: 1.1.1
define('DN_CONTROLLER_VERSION', '1.1.1');
const VERSION = '1.1.1';
```

Exception: pure docs / `.cursor` rules / git-only changes that do not affect plugin runtime do not require a version bump.
